<title>GERMANY: Waigel sees German 1997 deficit at 3.0 pct of GDP.</title>
<headline>Waigel sees German 1997 deficit at 3.0 pct of GDP.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Friday that Germany's total public sector deficit in 1997 would be 110 billion marks, or 3.0 percent of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>That would put Germany in line to fulfil the Maastricht Treaty criterion for budget deficits in countries participating in Europe's monetary union, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Germany will fulfil the Maastricht deficit criterion,&quot; Waigel told a news conference after the cabinet approved his 1998 draft budget and supplementary budget for 1997.</p>
</text>
